      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] Implement a numerical experiment to measure the constraint capacity $N_c(w)$ of small feedforward networks under varying constraint counts $w$. This involves generating abstract constraints (e.g., polynomial interpolation tasks), training networks with varied hidden layer widths, and determining the minimum width required to achieve zero violation on held-out constraints. The output will be a dataset plotting $N_c(w)$ vs $w$ to test for rigidity (flat trend) vs. fatter solution space (increasing trend)."
